column5:
After arranging everything with Damek, Gryz returned to his office.{w}
He had a lot to do, working with both The Rebellion and The Triumvirate.{w}
Though his true allegiance was with the rebels, he had to keep up appearances.{w}
That meant trying to strike an allegiance with the most unexpected of factions.

column6:
和达梅克安排妥当后，格瑞兹回到了自己的办公室。{w}
他要做的事很多，既要应付反抗军，又要应付三人执政团。{w}
虽然他真正效忠的是反抗军，但表面上得装装样子。{w}
那就意味着，他得设法和一个最意想不到的势力结盟。

column5:
When I exit my house, I feel a wave of heat overtake me.{w}
The sun pierces through the canopy of Valinorth with fierce intensity.{w}
Some of the residents use makeshift fans, looking utterly exhausted.{w}
Fortaime, however, stands there unaffected, with a huge smile on his face.

column6:
我走出家门，一股热浪扑面而来。{w}
烈日猛烈地穿透瓦利诺斯的树冠。{w}
一些居民摇着简易扇子，看起来疲惫不堪。{w}
可福泰姆却若无其事地站在那儿，脸上挂着大大的笑容。

column5:
Fortaime has now permanently joined your party.{w}
A comrade joining your party also retroactively unlocks content.{w}
For example, you can bring Fortaime to your home and talk to him there.{w}
It is a good idea to form a habit of revisiting previous areas.

column6:
福泰姆现已永久加入你的队伍。{w}
同伴加入队伍还会追溯性地解锁内容。{w}
例如，你可以带福泰姆回家，在那里和他交谈。{w}
养成重访旧区域的习惯是个好主意。

column5:
The higher up you live, the more you have to pay.{w}
Houses up there, with great views, are way too expensive.{w}
Of course, The Elder happily lives above everybody else.{w}
Thankfully, that's not reflected in the way he treats us.

column6:
住得越高，花费就越多。{w}
上面的房子视野绝佳，价格也贵得离谱。{w}
当然，长老乐呵呵地住在所有人之上。{w}
好在，他待我们的方式并没有沾上那股高高在上。

column5:
I notice the streams of water are in full flow today.{w}
We siphon off water from falls higher up in the mountains.{w}
That's how we fill the water tank each and every day.{w}
Each morning, every citizen does a "water run", so to speak.

column6:
我注意到今天水流淌得满满当当。{w}
我们从山上更高处的瀑布引水。{w}
我们每天就是这样把水塔灌满的。{w}
每天早晨，每个村民都要跑一趟“取水”，可以这么说。

column5:
These runs are a requirement for everyone in Valinorth.{w}
Without them, the tank would overflow and flood our village.{w}
I should do mine before it gets too late, actually.{w}
One person might not matter, but that's a bad mentality.

column6:
在瓦利诺斯，每个人都必须参加取水。{w}
要是没人做，水塔就会溢出，淹没我们的村庄。{w}
其实我该趁早去完成自己那份。{w}
少一个人或许无关紧要，但那种心态很要不得。

column5:
I must be blessed with peaceful neighbors.{w}
I've never heard a single peep come from next door.{w}
Fortaime is loud, but thankfully he lives across the street.{w}
With him next door, I'd probably die of sleep deprivation.

column6:
我大概是摊上了安静的邻居。{w}
隔壁一点动静都没听到过。{w}
福泰姆嗓门大，好在他住在街对面。{w}
要是他住隔壁，我恐怕得因睡眠不足而死。

column5:
That's Valinorth's post office at the end of the road.{w}
Village-wide notices are posted there, and we all have boxes.{w}
Sometimes it's easier to catch someone by mail when they're busy.{w}
I haven't checked my box in a while, but I rarely get any messages.

column6:
路尽头的那个是瓦利诺斯的邮局。{w}
全村的公告都贴在那里，我们每人都有一个信箱。{w}
有时候别人忙，寄信反而更容易找到他们。{w}
我有一阵子没查看信箱了，不过我本来就很少收到信。

column5:
I only really interact with Valessa and Fortaime.{w}
We can't carry out our duties unless we're together in person.{w}
If I got mail from someone else, it would likely be junk.{w}
If Mylus needed me, he'd come to me in person too.

column6:
我真正有来往的，也就瓦莱莎和福泰姆。{w}
不聚在一起，我们就没法履行职责。{w}
要是收到别人的来信，多半也是些没用的东西。{w}
迈勒斯要是需要我，也会亲自来找我。

column5:
I wonder why the spirits are getting stronger.{w}
Or, maybe their grip on my mind is getting stronger.{w}
Either way, a lot of books on them are outdated.{w}
Even Fortaime is struggling to catch up.

column6:
不知道灵体为什么会越来越强。{w}
又或者，是它们对我心智的钳制越来越紧。{w}
不管怎样，关于它们的书很多都过时了。{w}
连福泰姆都快跟不上了。

column5:
This is Fortaime's house, and it's in tip-top condition.{w}
It looks brand new, he must take very good care of it.{w}
As I get closer, I notice a book left out on his porch.{w}
It has his name on the front, so I can only assume it's his own work.

column6:
这是福泰姆的家，状态好得没话说。{w}
看起来跟新的一样，他一定很爱惜。{w}
走近些，我注意到他家门廊上放着一本书。{w}
封面上有他的名字，我只能猜那是他自己的作品。

column5:
In Valinorth, we're very in tune with the spirits.{w}
Many believe that's because we're surrounded by nature.{w}
That is, however, except for the stretches of road we created.{w}
They're semi-recent, and they caused a pretty large uproar.

column6:
在瓦利诺斯，我们与灵体非常契合。{w}
许多人相信，这是因为我们被自然环绕。{w}
不过，我们自己修的那几段路算是例外。{w}
它们是近些年才建的，当时引起了相当大的争议。

column5:
Some thought it would lead to more and more deforestation.{w}
Thankfully, it never escalated, and became very convenient.{w}
It didn't harm our connection with the spirits, either.{w}
In fact, over time, that bond only appears to get stronger.

column6:
有人担心这会导致越来越多的滥伐。{w}
还好事情没有恶化，反而带来了极大的便利。{w}
也没有损害我们与灵体的联系。{w}
事实上，随着时间推移，这份羁绊似乎只增不减。

column5:
Pro slammed his hand of cards down on the table.{w}
His opponents scoffed, and shouted accusations of cheating.{w}
He smirked as he made his way to the bar, laughing them off.{w}
With his newfound riches, he'd celebrate over a drink.

column6:
普洛把手里那副牌重重摔在桌上。{w}
他的对手嗤之以鼻，大喊他出老千。{w}
他咧嘴轻笑，一边走向吧台，一边把那些话当耳旁风。{w}
靠着新到手的钱财，他要喝一杯庆祝庆祝。

column5:
Valessa has now permanently joined your party.{w}
Like before, new content has been unlocked in old areas.{w}
But a new feature, "Parallel Chronicles", has also been unlocked.{w}
A brief tutorial on that will follow after this dialogue window.

column6:
瓦莱莎现已永久加入你的队伍。{w}
和之前一样，旧区域中解锁了新内容。{w}
此外还解锁了一项新功能——“平行编年史”。{w}
本对话框结束后，会有简短的教学说明。

column5:
Houses near the tank are reserved for the elderly.{w}
Something about minimizing travel time to our water source.{w}
Of course, houses near here are way too humid to be comfortable.{w}
But for some reason, they don't complain, and happily reside inside.

column6:
水塔附近的房子是留给老人的。{w}
据说是为了缩短他们到水源的路程。{w}
当然，这附近的房子潮得根本住不舒服。{w}
可不知为何，他们毫无怨言，还乐呵呵地住在里面。

column5:
These eaves carry water from the falls to the tank.{w}
It's completely self-sustaining, and requires little upkeep.{w}
We just have to empty the tank each morning to get our fill.{w}
It's something we can't live without, so it never goes unused.

column6:
这些引水檐把瀑布的水引到水塔。{w}
整套系统完全自给自足，几乎不用维护。{w}
我们只要每天早上把水塔排空，取够自家用的水。{w}
这是不可或缺的东西，所以从不闲置。

column5:
Water runs down the side of the tanks at a steady rate.{w}
That's a sign that it's gotten full, and requires attention.{w}
For a moment I'm glad that so much water is in the center of Valinorth.{w}
If we could somehow redirect the flow, it could easily combat fire.

column6:
水匀速地从水塔侧面淌下。{w}
这说明水塔已满，需要处理。{w}
有那么一瞬间，我很庆幸瓦利诺斯的中心有这么多水。{w}
要是能想办法改变水流的方向，灭火轻而易举。

column5:
Sovy entered the chambers of The Triumvirate unprompted.{w}
For Halin had extracted the information they desired.{w}
They raised their hoods and turned to him, scoffing.{w}
A hint of aggression on their quickly concealed faces.

column6:
索维未经传召便闯入了三人执政团的内室。{w}
因为哈林已经问出了他们想要的情报。{w}
他们拉起兜帽，转身对着他嗤笑。{w}
他们迅速掩饰的脸上，闪过一丝敌意。
